<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 5.9 Exercises</heading>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, determine if the points are solutions to the given system of equations.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="1" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x - 6y} &amp; = &amp; 0 \\ {3x - 4y} &amp; = &amp; 5 \end{matrix} \right. \begin{array}{l} { \text{A:} (3,1)} \\ { \text{B:} ( - 3,4)} \end{array}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="2" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- 3x + y} &amp; = &amp; 8 \\ {- x + 2y} &amp; = &amp; {- 9} \end{matrix} \right. \begin{array}{l} { \text{A:} ( - 5, - 7)} \\ { \text{B:} ( - 5,7)} \end{array}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="3" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + y} &amp; = &amp; 2 \\ y &amp; = &amp; {\frac{3}{4}x} \end{matrix} \right. \begin{array}{l} { \text{A:} \left( {\frac{8}{7},\frac{6}{7}} \right)} \\ { \text{B:} \left( {1,\frac{3}{4}} \right)} \end{array}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="4" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 6 \\ y &amp; = &amp; {\frac{2}{3}x + 2} \end{matrix} \right. \begin{array}{l} { \text{A:} ( - 6,2)} \\ { \text{B:} ( - 3,4)} \end{array}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the following systems of equations by graphing.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="5" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- x + y} &amp; = &amp; 2 \\ {2x + y} &amp; = &amp; {- 4} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="6" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} y &amp; = &amp; {x - 2} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- 3x + 2} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="7" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} y &amp; = &amp; {\frac{2}{3}x - 2} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{1}{3}x - 5} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="8" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 3 \\ {x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 3 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="9" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x - y} &amp; = &amp; 4 \\ {2x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 12 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="10" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- x + 2y} &amp; = &amp; {- 6} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{1}{2}x - 1} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="11" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {3x + 5y} &amp; = &amp; 10 \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{3}{5}x + 1} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="12" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {4x} &amp; = &amp; {3y + 7} \\ {8x - 6y} &amp; = &amp; 14 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the systems of equations by substitution.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="13" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x + y} &amp; = &amp; {- 4} \\ {3x - 2y} &amp; = &amp; {- 6} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="14" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x + y} &amp; = &amp; {- 2} \\ {3x - y} &amp; = &amp; 7 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="15" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x - 2y} &amp; {=} &amp; {- 5} \\ {2x - 3y} &amp; {=} &amp; {- 4} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="16" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x - 3y} &amp; {=} &amp; {- 9} \\ {2x + 5y} &amp; {=} &amp; 4 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="17" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- 2x + 2y} &amp; {=} &amp; 6 \\ { y} &amp; {=} &amp; {- 3x + 1} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="18" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {3x + 4y} &amp; = &amp; 1 \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{2}{5}x + 2} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="19" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} x &amp; = &amp; {2y} \\ {4x - 8y} &amp; = &amp; 0 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="20" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} y &amp; = &amp; {\frac{7}{8}x + 4} \\ {- 7x + 8y} &amp; = &amp; 6 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the systems of equations by elimination.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="21" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {5x + 2y} &amp; = &amp; 2 \\ {- 3x - y} &amp; = &amp; 0 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="22" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {6x - 5y} &amp; = &amp; {- 1} \\ {2x + y} &amp; = &amp; 13 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="23" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {2x - 5y} &amp; = &amp; 7 \\ {3x - y} &amp; = &amp; 17 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="24" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {5x - 3y} &amp; = &amp; {- 1} \\ {2x - y} &amp; = &amp; 2 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="25" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {3x - 5y} &amp; = &amp; {- 9} \\ {5x + 2y} &amp; = &amp; 16 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="26" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {\frac{1}{3}x - y} &amp; = &amp; {- 3} \\ {x + \frac{5}{2}y} &amp; = &amp; 2 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="27" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {6x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 9 \\ {2x + y} &amp; = &amp; 3 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="28" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {\frac{2}{3}x + y} &amp; = &amp; 5 \\ {2x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 11 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, solve the system of equations by graphing, substitution, or elimination.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="29" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {3x + y} &amp; = &amp; {- 3} \\ {2x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 5 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="30" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} y &amp; = &amp; {x + 2} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- 2x + 2} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="31" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} y &amp; = &amp; {\frac{3}{2}x + 1} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{1}{2}x + 5} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="32" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + y} &amp; = &amp; {- 4} \\ {- x + 2y} &amp; = &amp; {- 2} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="33" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {- 2x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 3 \\ {x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; 12 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="34" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {x + 3y} &amp; = &amp; {- 6} \\ y &amp; = &amp; {- \frac{4}{3}x + 4} \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="35" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} {4x - 3y} &amp; = &amp; 8 \\ {8x - 6y} &amp; = &amp; 14 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="36" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\left\{ \begin{matrix} x &amp; = &amp; {- 3y + 4} \\ {2x + 6y} &amp; = &amp; 8 \end{matrix} \right.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>For the following exercises, translate to a system of equations and solve.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="37" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Jackie has been offered positions by two cable companies. The first company pays a salary of \$14,000 plus a commission of \$100 for each cable package sold. The second pays a salary of \$20,000 plus a commission of \$25 for each cable package sold. How many cable packages would need to be sold to make the total pay the same?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="38" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Drew burned 1,800 calories Friday playing 1 hour of basketball and canoeing for 2 hours. Saturday she spent 2 hours playing basketball and 3 hours canoeing and burned 3,200 calories. How many calories did she burn per hour when playing basketball? How many calories did she burn per hour when canoeing?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="39" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Mitchell currently sells stoves for company A at a salary of \$12,000 plus a \$150 commission for each stove he sells. Company B offers him a position with a salary of \$24,000 plus a \$50 commission for each stove he sells. How many stoves would Mitchell need to sell for the options to equal?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="40" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>The total number of calories in 2 hot dogs and 3 cups of cottage cheese is 960 calories. The total number of calories in 5 hot dogs and 2 cups of cottage cheese is 1,190 calories. How many calories are in a hot dog? How many calories are in a cup of cottage cheese?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="41" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Andrea and Bart go to the local farmers market to purchase some fruit. Andrea buys 4 apples and 5 oranges, which cost \$3.10; Bart buys 4 apples and 6 oranges, which cost \$3.40. What is the cost of an orange? What is the cost of an apple?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="42" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Jack and Jill go to a local farmers market to purchase some fruit. Jack buys 3 peaches and 2 limes, which cost \$1.50; Jill buys 6 peaches and 5 limes, which cost \$3.45. What is the cost of a peach? What is the cost of a lime?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
  </exercises>
</section>
